  "commit_message": "GOV-12: Alias Canon & DSCI Integration - Complete\n\n✅ Database & Backend (GOV-12 Phase 1):\n- Created canonical aliases table with AUTO/RELATIONSHIP/MASK taxonomy\n- Added alias_type constraint and corporeal_auto enforcement\n- Implemented Alias domain model with helper methods\n- Created AliasRepository with full CRUD operations\n- Implemented AliasService with semantic enforcement:\n  - EnsureCorporealRootAlias for corporeal domains (idempotent)\n  - EnsureStructuralAlias for seat instantiation (idempotent)\n  - CreateRelationshipAlias for volitional identity (conflict detection)\n  - CreateMaskAlias for ephemeral browsing (name auto-generation)\n- Added database views for alias analytics\n- Prepared DSCI contract linkage (pending contracts table)\n\n✅ API & Receipt Integration (GOV-12 Phase 2):\n- Implemented 3 REST endpoints:\n  - GET /api/domain/:id/aliases (with type filter)\n  - POST /api/domain/:id/alias/relationship\n  - POST /api/domain/:id/alias/mask\n- Wired receipt integration using GOV-10 identity receipt system\n- Created alias receipt helpers (RecordAliasAddReceipt, RecordAliasRetireReceipt)\n\n✅ Comprehensive Testing (GOV-12 Phase 3):\n- Domain model tests: validation, type checkers, metadata helpers\n- Repository tests: CRUD, constraint enforcement, name reuse after retirement\n- Service tests: idempotency, conflict detection, name generation\n- API tests: success paths, validation errors, conflict handling\n\n✅ Documentation:\n- docs/GOV12_ALIAS_CANON.md (650 lines)\n- phases/GOV12_HANDOFF.json (complete)\n- Documented REGO policy hooks for future enforcement\n\nAll GOV-12 objectives complete. Ready for GOV-13 (Contracts & DSCI Wiring).",

